# Signing configuration for release builds (scripts/build-release-arm64.sh or
# the Android Studio run configuration "Release APK (arm64)").
#
# === One-time key setup ===
#
# 1. Open a terminal in the project directory (Android Studio: View > Tool Windows > Terminal).
#
# 2. Create a keystore and key. keytool comes with the JDK; if it is not on PATH,
#    Android Studio ships it at <Android Studio>/jbr/bin/keytool:
#
#      keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore camperlog-release.jks -alias camperlog \
#              -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#
#    keytool asks for a password (at least six characters) and identity details.
#    Confirm with "yes" at the end. Since Java 9, the keystore password also
#    protects the key; use the same value for both password fields below.
#
# 3. Copy this file to keystore.properties and fill in the passwords:
#
#      cp keystore.properties.example keystore.properties
#
# 4. Test with scripts/build-release-arm64.sh --no-install.
#    Output: app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - camperlog-release.jks and keystore.properties are ignored by Git (.gitignore).
# - Back up both securely. Without the same key, installed apps cannot be updated;
#   reinstalling instead would delete stored tours.
# - For GitHub Actions, encode a copy with storeFile=release.jks; see README.md.
#
# storeFile is relative to the project directory or an absolute path.
storeFile=camperlog-release.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=camperlog
keyPassword=
